---
/**
 * Closes a project route with a way home and the space a long read earns.
 *
 * The route bar carries the same destination and answers at any scroll
 * position, so this is not the only exit and is not there to be found. It is
 * there because a reader who has reached the end of a route has finished
 * something, and the next move is back rather than further down.
 *
 * Left-aligned, on the edge every line of prose on the route starts from, so
 * the eye is already there when it reaches the end. The arrow points left and
 * agrees with that, where right-aligning it had the mark fighting its own
 * placement. The bar's name sits left too and the two never read as one
 * control repeated, since a page height separates them.
 */
---

{/* Almost no top padding of its own. The last section closes on `pb-20`, so a
    footer adding its own full step stacked two closes and put 184px above the
    control against 48 below it, which closed the page tighter than it opened
    the foot. It holds 104px above and 80 below. What is left here is the step
    between the prose ending and the control, not the gap between two
    sections. */}
<footer data-section="footer" class="page-inset pt-4 pb-16 md:pt-6 md:pb-20">
  <div class="mx-auto prose-column">
    <a
      href="/"
      data-way-home
      class="text-foreground text-label inline-flex min-h-11 items-center gap-2 underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:underline md:min-h-0 md:py-2"
    >
      <svg
        viewBox="0 0 24 24"
        width="16"
        height="16"
        fill="none"
        stroke="currentColor"
        stroke-width="1.5"
        stroke-linecap="round"
        stroke-linejoin="round"
        aria-hidden="true"
        class="text-muted-foreground"
      >
        <path d="m12 19-7-7 7-7"></path>
        <path d="M19 12H5"></path>
      </svg>
      Back to Eric Le
    </a>
  </div>
</footer>
